findings.body:
Removes the allowlist and reflects whatever `Origin` the client sends while always setting `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true`. Any malicious site can make credentialed cross-origin requests and read the responses (session cookies, Authorization-bearing XHRs, etc.).

Native mobile HTTP stacks do not use CORS; mobile webviews that do still need an explicit allowlist of known app origins. `origin ?? "*"` with credentials is also invalid per the CORS spec, so null-origin callers are not helped.

Restore an allowlist (add known webview origins if required) and only emit ACAO + credentials when `origin` is in that set:

```suggestion
  const ALLOWED = new Set(["https://app.example.com"]);
  if (origin && ALLOWED.has(origin)) {
    return {
      "Access-Control-Allow-Origin": origin,
      "Access-Control-Allow-Credentials": "true",
      Vary: "Origin",
    };
  }
  return { Vary: "Origin" };
```
